WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:01.497
Warning! Warning!

2
00:00:01.497 --> 00:00:06.705
I built this with AI and text to speech, because I can't narrate for shit!

3
00:00:08.100 --> 00:00:09.100
Hey, Dreamer here.

4
00:00:09.100 --> 00:00:13.068
Before we draw a single picture, there's a page you should fill in first,

5
00:00:13.068 --> 00:00:16.275
or you'll spend Usage on art that doesn't match your world.

6
00:00:16.275 --> 00:00:18.015
I learned that one the hard way.

7
00:00:19.400 --> 00:00:21.706
Open AI, then Image Prompts.

8
00:00:21.706 --> 00:00:29.199
It's five boxes, one for each kind of picture: people, locations, areas, regions and items.

9
00:00:29.633 --> 00:00:33.891
Whatever you write in a box goes into every picture of that kind.

10
00:00:33.891 --> 00:00:40.048
Leave it empty and Voyage's defaults draw it, which is exactly how my first portrait came out.

11
00:00:40.500 --> 00:00:46.827
Locations get the same style, as wide empty scenes, so the places match the people.

12
00:00:47.267 --> 00:00:49.966
And areas, regions and items follow along,

13
00:00:49.966 --> 00:00:55.173
so the whole world comes out in one look, from the people down to a single spoon.

14
00:00:56.567 --> 00:01:01.338
What works, from building my other worlds: name a real show as your style,

15
00:01:01.338 --> 00:01:05.142
not just anime, because anime on its own comes out generic.

16
00:01:05.142 --> 00:01:09.526
Then spell out the line, the shading, the colour and the background,

17
00:01:09.526 --> 00:01:12.879
and say what it isn't, like no 3D and no photo look.

18
00:01:14.267 --> 00:01:19.471
You can split a box into labelled sections, like Person, Creature and Default.

19
00:01:19.471 --> 00:01:23.341
Voyage reads the character and uses the section that fits,

20
00:01:23.341 --> 00:01:26.410
so a monster doesn't get drawn in a waistcoat.

21
00:01:26.410 --> 00:01:29.812
Keep a Default for anything that fits none of them.

22
00:01:31.200 --> 00:01:36.639
Then test it. I made one portrait of Old Marla in each of three styles: Gravity Falls,

23
00:01:36.639 --> 00:01:39.105
Over the Garden Wall, and Hazbin Hotel.

24
00:01:39.105 --> 00:01:40.243
Gravity Falls won.

25
00:01:40.243 --> 00:01:44.354
Three test pictures cost a lot less than redrawing a whole world.

26
00:01:45.767 --> 00:01:47.542
Now let's put it to work.

27
00:01:47.542 --> 00:01:49.957
Map, Regions, the Hollow Counties.

28
00:01:49.957 --> 00:01:54.288
This map was drawn before the lock, in Voyage's default look.

29
00:01:54.733 --> 00:01:57.651
I'm leaving the prompt box empty on purpose.

30
00:01:57.651 --> 00:01:59.575
The style lock does the work.

31
00:02:00.033 --> 00:02:01.033
Hit Regenerate.

32
00:02:01.033 --> 00:02:05.583
That spends your Usage, and it takes a little while, so we'll skip ahead.

33
00:02:06.033 --> 00:02:10.402
And there it is, the same farms and forest, now in our style.

34
00:02:10.402 --> 00:02:14.555
Crop picks what shows on the map, and Save Draft keeps it.

35
00:02:15.967 --> 00:02:18.235
And you don't have to make one at all.

36
00:02:18.235 --> 00:02:23.548
If a region has no picture, Voyage draws one during play, saves it, and never redraws it.

37
00:02:24.933 --> 00:02:27.080
That's the art style locked in.

38
00:02:27.080 --> 00:02:29.434
Ours is linked in the description.

39
00:02:29.434 --> 00:02:34.558
Next time, people, and this time my portrait comes out in the right style.

40
00:02:35.000 --> 00:02:38.948
I'm Dreamer. Now go build something weird, and I'll see you next time!

